.TH SHOAL-DOCTOR 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-doctor \- diagnose a Shoal installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-doctor
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks platform support, paths, permissions, layered configuration, sandboxing,
and the installed companion executables.
All checks run so an early failure does not hide later findings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the complete machine-readable report instead of the human checklist.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Human output groups checks by status.
JSON output includes every result and its severity for automation.
.SH ERRORS
Failed installation checks are represented in the report and final status.
Invalid arguments or a JSON rendering failure are command errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-doctor
shoal-doctor --json
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when required checks pass, 1 when required checks fail, and 2 for invalid arguments or report rendering failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1),
.BR shoal-landlock-helper (1)
